WEBVTT

00:07.050 --> 00:11.680
[MIKASA] Everyone keeps saying
Eren has changed.

00:11.760 --> 00:14.220
And I thought he had, too.

00:14.310 --> 00:15.930
But...

00:16.020 --> 00:20.020
I wonder if we've
all got it wrong.

00:31.860 --> 00:34.450
[MIKASA]
It could be that he's always

00:34.530 --> 00:37.750
been like this inside.

00:37.830 --> 00:41.120
But if this is
the real Eren Jaeger...

00:41.210 --> 00:46.460
...what did I see in him
that made me keep him so close?

01:00.640 --> 01:02.150
Can you believe there are really

01:02.230 --> 01:05.070
enough people outside the walls
to fill up such a gigantic city?

01:05.150 --> 01:06.270
Try not to talk about the walls

01:06.360 --> 01:08.440
in front of the
general public, Conny.

01:08.530 --> 01:10.610
Ah, right. Sorry about that.

01:10.700 --> 01:12.950
[SASHA] This is the world
beyond the walls.

01:13.030 --> 01:14.990
We're finally here,
outside the walls

01:15.080 --> 01:16.450
we've known our whole lives.

01:16.540 --> 01:18.330
The walls no one
has ever escaped!

01:18.410 --> 01:20.830
Gah, would you
listen to me for once?

01:22.160 --> 01:24.210
If you think about it,
this is sort of

01:24.290 --> 01:27.170
a return to the
Scouts' original mission.

01:32.260 --> 01:34.390
[HANGE]
Let the survey begin.

01:49.990 --> 01:51.280
Ahh.

01:56.620 --> 01:57.910
[ONYANKOPON]
My friends!

01:57.990 --> 02:00.870
I'd like to welcome you
to the continent of Marley!

02:00.950 --> 02:04.460
The Azumabito have been waiting.
May I escort you?

02:04.540 --> 02:05.830
Hey, Onyankopon!

02:05.920 --> 02:09.250
[ONYANKOPON laughs] It's so good
to see you all here!

02:09.340 --> 02:10.800
So, what does
everyone think about

02:10.880 --> 02:12.760
the biggest port in the country?

02:12.840 --> 02:15.180
[CONNY gasps]
What's with that horse?

02:15.260 --> 02:17.390
Or, wait. Is that--
What was that?

02:17.470 --> 02:19.680
Nah. No horse ever
looked like that.

02:19.770 --> 02:20.930
I think it was a Marleyan cow!

02:21.020 --> 02:22.430
[HANGE]
It must've been a car.

02:22.520 --> 02:24.140
I've definitely
heard about those!

02:24.230 --> 02:26.480
Hey! Car! Here, boy!

02:26.560 --> 02:28.230
They're making a scene.
Everyone's staring!

02:28.310 --> 02:30.610
[JEAN sighs] All these
people are gonna think

02:30.690 --> 02:32.360
we're a bunch of yokels now.

02:32.440 --> 02:33.400
[ARMIN gasps]

02:33.490 --> 02:34.950
Just act like
you don't know him.

02:35.030 --> 02:38.740
[HANGE] Come back, car!
I promise I'll be nice!

02:38.830 --> 02:40.620
Better get them on a leash.

02:40.700 --> 02:41.950
They'll try and
feed the car carrots

02:42.040 --> 02:43.500
if they manage to catch it.

02:43.580 --> 02:45.540
[ONYANKOPON laughs]
Give him more credit than tha--

02:45.620 --> 02:47.500
Wait, are they buying carrots?

02:47.580 --> 02:49.340
There are so many people here.

02:49.420 --> 02:50.750
Stay near me, Eren.

02:50.840 --> 02:52.800
We have no idea what to expect.

02:52.880 --> 02:55.260
You're safest at my side.

02:56.340 --> 02:58.390
You all right?

02:58.470 --> 03:00.100
Yeah, got it.

03:00.180 --> 03:02.600
[ARMIN] This is no time
to be spacing out, Eren!

03:02.680 --> 03:05.520
We finally reached
the outside world!

03:07.690 --> 03:11.070
We really made it
across the sea, huh?

03:11.150 --> 03:12.860
We're here.

03:14.700 --> 03:17.610
[LEVI]
Guys. Stick with the group.

03:17.700 --> 03:19.620
Especially you, Eren.

03:19.700 --> 03:21.120
Be right there!

03:27.290 --> 03:28.250
[CIVILIAN 87A gasps]

03:28.330 --> 03:30.670
Hey, watch where
you're walking, kid!

03:32.710 --> 03:35.380
May I please have one?

03:35.460 --> 03:37.180
But, of course!

03:39.140 --> 03:40.050
[VENDOR 87A]
Here. Enjoy!

03:40.140 --> 03:43.140
Whoa! Sasha!
Show some restraint!

03:46.230 --> 03:48.440
[SASHA gasps]
How is it cold like that?

03:48.520 --> 03:49.860
[CONNY]
I wanna try it!

03:49.940 --> 03:51.980
I take it this is your
first time tasting ice cream!

03:52.060 --> 03:53.270
What is this stuff made of?

03:53.360 --> 03:55.230
I'd like one, too, please, sir!

03:55.320 --> 03:56.490
[CONNY]
Me, too!

03:56.570 --> 03:59.410
Those idiots. I told 'em
not to draw attention.

03:59.490 --> 04:01.320
They stick out,
but they won't look like

04:01.410 --> 04:04.040
island devils if they're
acting like overgrown kids.

04:04.120 --> 04:07.710
You guys. I swear you've never
tasted anything like this!

04:09.000 --> 04:12.920
[CLOWN 87A] Hi, little fella.
Got some tasty candy for ya.

04:13.000 --> 04:14.920
Wanna try it?

04:20.140 --> 04:23.140
It's real good.

04:24.640 --> 04:26.180
Sharp suit there, bud.

04:26.270 --> 04:28.100
Are you and your friends
playing gangster?

04:28.190 --> 04:29.560
[SASHA] There's something
delicious off yonder!

04:29.640 --> 04:31.310
[CONNY] What if that's
the thing Nicolo mentioned?

04:31.400 --> 04:32.940
[JEAN]
Hey! Three more, please!

04:33.020 --> 04:34.480
Sure thing.

04:37.610 --> 04:41.450
[MIKASA] Eren.
You really need to taste this.

04:41.530 --> 04:42.870
It's ice cream, right?

04:42.950 --> 04:45.830
[MIKASA]
Uh-- You know about it?

04:45.910 --> 04:48.750
I think I saw it somewhere
in Dad's memories.

04:48.830 --> 04:52.330
Eldians in the internment zones
usually can't get it.

04:53.670 --> 04:54.960
The outside world's massive,

04:55.040 --> 04:57.550
but they don't want us
to be part of it.

04:59.920 --> 05:02.890
[MIKASA] We didn't
recognize it at the time.

05:02.970 --> 05:08.220
Or maybe we refused to
let ourselves accept it.

05:10.690 --> 05:13.940
[LEVI] Hey! I don't think
that purse belongs to you,

05:14.020 --> 05:14.980
does it, kid?

05:15.070 --> 05:16.110
[RAMZI gasps]

05:16.190 --> 05:18.440
Huh? [Gasps]

05:18.530 --> 05:19.650
[CIVILIAN 87A]
Thief!

05:19.740 --> 05:21.950
Well, look at that.
Another enemy immigrant!

05:22.030 --> 05:23.700
[CIVILIAN 87C]
How'd you get into Marley?

05:23.780 --> 05:25.410
[CIVILIAN 87D]
Bet he stowed away on a ship!

05:25.490 --> 05:27.240
[CIVILIAN 87E]
He can't understand us, can he?

05:27.330 --> 05:29.080
[CIVILIAN 87A]
We could toss him into the sea!

05:29.160 --> 05:31.540
[CIVILIAN 87C]
Nah. I say we smash his hands.

05:31.620 --> 05:34.000
That oughta stop him
from picking pockets.

05:34.080 --> 05:35.500
[CIVILIAN 87E] Why don't we
string the little rat up

05:35.580 --> 05:37.250
somewhere everyone can see him?

05:37.340 --> 05:39.050
It'll scare off the next thief!

05:39.130 --> 05:41.670
There's no need!
Don't hurt him, okay?

05:41.760 --> 05:44.050
I got my purse back,
so why go that far?

05:44.140 --> 05:46.640
Young lady, this is about
more than just your purse.

05:46.720 --> 05:48.180
All us merchants
working in this port

05:48.270 --> 05:50.020
are trying to make
an honest living.

05:50.100 --> 05:51.810
We can't allow the riffraff
to run around

05:51.890 --> 05:53.440
stealing from our customers!

05:53.520 --> 05:56.060
On top of that, this kid
could be a Subject of Ymir.

05:56.150 --> 05:57.570
[SASHA gasps]

05:57.650 --> 05:59.070
[CIVILIAN 87F] Blood testing has
been picking up like crazy

05:59.150 --> 06:01.240
all over during
the past few years.

06:01.320 --> 06:02.820
Now that we know
the devils have been

06:02.900 --> 06:06.700
blending in with the rest of us,
people are losing sleep over it!

06:11.250 --> 06:14.580
[CIVILIAN 87H] Hey! What do
you think you're doing?

06:14.670 --> 06:17.080
[LEVI] I never said
he was a pickpocket.

06:17.170 --> 06:20.460
All I said was the purse
didn't belong to him.

06:20.550 --> 06:23.470
He owes his big sister an
apology for this little prank.

06:23.550 --> 06:24.340
[SASHA gasps]

06:24.430 --> 06:26.800
Jeez. That's children for ya!

06:26.890 --> 06:29.930
But what can ya do? Right?
It's a family thing!

06:30.020 --> 06:31.970
Huh? Oh! Yeah!

06:32.060 --> 06:35.270
I'm sorry my little brother
acted like an idiot, everybody!

06:35.350 --> 06:37.520
Smells like bullshit.
You think we're stupid?

06:37.610 --> 06:38.900
Run for it!

06:41.110 --> 06:42.990
[CIVILIAN 87I]
Hey! Come back!

06:47.320 --> 06:53.580
[ALL panting]

06:55.460 --> 06:57.500
Did anyone see where
the brat ran off to?

06:57.580 --> 07:00.090
Oh. He's right there.

07:02.590 --> 07:03.800
[LEVI gasps]

07:05.470 --> 07:06.550
[LEVI]
Well, then.

07:06.640 --> 07:09.510
So much for the
Azumabito's pocket change.

07:14.230 --> 07:17.230
[KIYOMI] I'm sorry you
had to go through that.

07:17.310 --> 07:19.940
With improvements in
blood testing technology,

07:20.020 --> 07:22.650
countries are beginning to
discover that Subjects of Ymir

07:22.730 --> 07:25.570
have been able to sneak out
of the internment zones

07:25.650 --> 07:28.530
and blend into
the wider population.

07:28.620 --> 07:29.990
The bloodline of Ymir
made its way

07:30.080 --> 07:32.120
across Eldian territory
when the empire was

07:32.200 --> 07:34.370
at the height of its power,
and for many centuries,

07:34.450 --> 07:36.040
the ability to
trace one's lineage

07:36.120 --> 07:37.460
back to a Subject of Ymir

07:37.540 --> 07:40.460
served as proof of noble status
among the global elite.

07:40.540 --> 07:42.340
But as the Empire crumbled,

07:42.420 --> 07:44.420
the aristocrats who'd
been aligned with Eldia

07:44.510 --> 07:46.590
quickly found themselves exiled.

07:46.670 --> 07:49.050
Today, you witnessed
the way Eldians are

07:49.140 --> 07:51.430
typically treated
beyond the walls.

07:51.510 --> 07:53.890
In light of that,
I'm sure you can see

07:53.970 --> 07:56.270
how difficult it will be
to convince the world

07:56.350 --> 08:00.350
to engage with the people of
Paradis on friendly terms.

08:03.520 --> 08:04.730
[ARMIN]
Even so.

08:04.820 --> 08:07.200
If we give up on pursuing
peace at this point,

08:07.280 --> 08:09.030
our only remaining option
will be to throw in

08:09.110 --> 08:11.280
with Zeke and his conspiracy.

08:11.370 --> 08:14.160
We would be leaving
our fates entirely up to him

08:14.240 --> 08:18.460
and sacrificing Historia's life,
and the lives of her children.

08:18.540 --> 08:19.920
That's right.

08:20.000 --> 08:22.040
We're looking for a way
to avoid such a future,

08:22.130 --> 08:24.340
and our search
brought us to Marley.

08:24.420 --> 08:26.800
This "Subject of Ymir
Protection Group"

08:26.880 --> 08:29.590
will be debuting at the
international forum tomorrow.

08:29.680 --> 08:31.090
They may be able to help.

08:31.180 --> 08:32.470
[KIYOMI]
It's possible.

08:32.550 --> 08:33.890
Though I would caution
against assuming

08:33.970 --> 08:36.060
your goals and theirs
are in alignment.

08:36.140 --> 08:38.060
[HANGE] We're not,
and we won't make contact

08:38.140 --> 08:40.350
until we've had a chance
to observe them.

08:40.440 --> 08:41.610
If they show promise,

08:41.690 --> 08:43.610
and if they'll agree to
hold a meeting with us,

08:43.690 --> 08:46.490
they can help us get our
message out into the world.

08:46.570 --> 08:47.820
You've come to
make it known that

08:47.900 --> 08:50.950
the people of Paradis
wish to coexist in peace?

08:51.030 --> 08:52.370
[HANGE]
Yes.

08:55.200 --> 08:57.870
[KIYOMI] Rest assured,
the Azumabito clan will

08:57.950 --> 09:00.710
happily aid you
in pursuing said goal.

09:00.790 --> 09:03.630
But... I must wonder
how realistic you've been

09:03.710 --> 09:05.500
in assessing
your odds of success.

09:05.590 --> 09:07.550
[HANGE gasps]

09:07.630 --> 09:11.550
Fact is, chances are slim
even if we do everything right.

09:11.640 --> 09:14.510
And we'll be in constant danger.

09:14.600 --> 09:17.350
But still, we at least
have to try.

09:17.430 --> 09:20.730
As long as there's a chance,
it's our duty to take it.

09:26.730 --> 09:29.530
Far be it from me
to tell you otherwise.

09:30.320 --> 09:32.410
[Gasps]

09:33.570 --> 09:34.910
[MIKASA gasps]

09:34.990 --> 09:37.370
Wait a minute. Where's Eren?

09:50.470 --> 09:53.800
[MIKASA panting]

09:53.890 --> 09:55.390
[MIKASA]
Eren!

09:56.640 --> 09:57.930
What are you thinking?

09:58.010 --> 10:00.350
Did you forget we're
undercover in enemy territory

10:00.430 --> 10:02.230
and you're their
number one target?

10:02.310 --> 10:04.730
Everyone's been
out looking for you.

10:09.900 --> 10:11.610
Is that the boy from the market?

10:11.690 --> 10:13.570
Did something happen here?

10:13.650 --> 10:16.120
No, nothing yet.

10:16.200 --> 10:19.910
[MIKASA]
What does that mean? Is this--

10:20.000 --> 10:21.450
[EREN]
These people are refugees who

10:21.540 --> 10:24.880
lost their homes
in Marley's wars.

10:24.960 --> 10:27.090
They're like us.

10:27.170 --> 10:30.300
The world they knew
before suddenly ended.

10:30.380 --> 10:33.010
Everything they had was taken.

10:33.090 --> 10:37.260
And the freedom they
enjoyed is long gone.

10:39.430 --> 10:42.890
Mikasa. I need to ask you

10:42.980 --> 10:46.400
why you care for me
as much as you do.

10:46.480 --> 10:47.610
[Gasps]

10:47.690 --> 10:49.320
Because I saved you?

10:49.400 --> 10:51.320
Back when we were little kids?

10:51.400 --> 10:54.450
Or is it more 'cause you
see me as family?

10:54.530 --> 10:56.370
[Gasps]

10:56.450 --> 10:59.410
Mikasa. What am I to you?

11:05.710 --> 11:07.040
Well...

11:07.960 --> 11:10.380
Y-You're my, uh...

11:10.460 --> 11:12.460
You're my family.

11:14.590 --> 11:15.880
[MIKASA gasps]

11:17.470 --> 11:19.720
[Speaking a foreign language]

11:19.800 --> 11:21.140
What?

11:21.220 --> 11:22.720
I think that was an invitation.

11:22.810 --> 11:24.140
[ARMIN]
Hey!

11:24.230 --> 11:26.480
What the hell do you think
you're doing, you maniac?

11:26.560 --> 11:28.560
[CONNY]
You some kinda moron?

11:29.480 --> 11:31.270
Perfect timing.

11:41.120 --> 11:43.910
[RAMZI'S GRANDPA chuckles]

11:49.290 --> 11:50.960
Ahh.

11:52.000 --> 11:54.670
[RAMZI'S GRANDPA laughs]

11:58.930 --> 12:00.260
[BOTH gasp]

12:56.940 --> 12:58.030
Ladies and gentlemen,

12:58.110 --> 13:00.110
this new organization
advocates for

13:00.200 --> 13:03.530
the Subjects of Ymir living as
refugees around the globe!

13:03.620 --> 13:05.870
These desperate people
are not responsible

13:05.950 --> 13:07.790
for the crimes of
the Eldian Empire,

13:07.870 --> 13:10.290
but rather,
its most tragic victims.

13:10.370 --> 13:12.290
The living legacy of
its effort to corrupt

13:12.380 --> 13:15.170
all the peoples of the world
with Eldian blood!

13:15.250 --> 13:18.340
The taint of Eldia is all but
cleansed from the earth.

13:18.420 --> 13:20.840
There's only one corner
where it continues to fester:

13:20.930 --> 13:22.390
the island of Paradis,

13:22.470 --> 13:24.510
where the empire's
most loyal subjects fled

13:24.600 --> 13:27.890
in the wake of Marley's victory
a hundred years ago.

13:27.970 --> 13:29.600
It is the island devils alone

13:29.680 --> 13:32.560
who pose a true
threat to humanity!

13:42.320 --> 13:43.660
[Gasps]

13:44.490 --> 13:50.200
[MIKASA] That was the day
when Eren truly left us.

13:50.290 --> 13:53.170
Later on, he would
send us a letter.

13:53.250 --> 13:57.340
He said he was going to
leave our futures up to Zeke.

13:57.420 --> 14:02.720
By the next time we saw him,
it was too late.

14:02.800 --> 14:05.140
Looking back,

14:05.220 --> 14:09.020
I still don't know if
there was some better way.

14:09.100 --> 14:11.430
Maybe everything had
already been decided

14:11.520 --> 14:13.980
from the start.

14:14.060 --> 14:16.810
But I can't help wondering.

14:16.900 --> 14:20.570
When he asked me
that question...

14:20.650 --> 14:23.530
...what if I'd given him
a different answer?

14:27.030 --> 14:30.330
[MIKASA] Would we still be
in this situation right now?

14:38.210 --> 14:40.710
[EREN]
Where did all of it begin?

14:42.130 --> 14:43.720
[EREN]
Was it there?

14:45.140 --> 14:48.970
[EREN]
No. It doesn't matter where.

14:56.270 --> 15:00.110
[EREN] Everything happened
as I willed it.

15:00.190 --> 15:03.650
Everything begins here.

15:06.950 --> 15:10.990
Eren. There's only one way
to break the cycle of violence

15:11.080 --> 15:12.910
for Eldia and the world.

15:13.000 --> 15:15.870
You must support
the euthanization plan.

15:15.960 --> 15:18.170
The brass won't be an obstacle.

15:18.250 --> 15:19.500
They've been
happily sipping away

15:19.590 --> 15:22.380
at that wine we tainted
with spinal fluid.

15:22.460 --> 15:25.300
You're a part of Zeke's plan
because he believes in you.

15:25.380 --> 15:28.100
Please return his faith.

15:28.180 --> 15:31.640
[EREN] For now, I'll pretend
to go along with Zeke's plot.

15:31.720 --> 15:33.180
You need to do the same.

15:33.270 --> 15:35.640
Keep your head down for a while.

15:35.730 --> 15:37.690
So we play along
with him for now,

15:37.770 --> 15:40.110
but what happens after that?

15:41.440 --> 15:44.860
[EREN] The MPs are still
pushing the same idea.

15:44.940 --> 15:48.780
They wanna turn you into a Titan
and have you eat Zeke.

15:48.870 --> 15:51.280
They're not gonna be
talked out of it.

15:51.370 --> 15:54.330
You can either fight or flee.

15:54.410 --> 15:56.330
[HISTORIA]
Since I came out here,

15:56.410 --> 16:00.040
I've had more to think about
than just raising cattle.

16:00.130 --> 16:02.040
I know what they're planning,

16:02.130 --> 16:05.470
but running and fighting
aren't my only options.

16:05.550 --> 16:06.920
If making me a Titan gives us

16:07.010 --> 16:09.720
the best chance of
saving the island,

16:09.800 --> 16:12.220
then I'm prepared to do it.

16:14.270 --> 16:17.270
Realistically,
it's the only way.

16:17.350 --> 16:19.600
Even so. I'm grateful.

16:19.690 --> 16:23.190
I've got friends who did
everything they could for me.

16:23.270 --> 16:25.940
You all fought hard
to protect me.

16:27.530 --> 16:30.320
[HISTORIA] It's enough
that you tried, I mean it.

16:31.410 --> 16:33.870
Maybe it is enough for you,
but not for me.

16:33.950 --> 16:35.330
[Gasps]

16:35.410 --> 16:39.250
I'll trample it to the ground--
the whole outside world.

16:39.330 --> 16:42.090
And every person in it.

16:42.170 --> 16:45.050
Men, women, children.
Every last one.

16:45.130 --> 16:46.710
That isn't the answer, Eren!

16:46.800 --> 16:48.880
Most of the people out there
don't have anything to do with

16:48.970 --> 16:50.300
what we've gone through!

16:50.390 --> 16:54.100
They would die ignorant
and terrified, like your mom.

16:54.180 --> 16:55.600
You'll be killing
innocent people

16:55.680 --> 16:58.350
for reasons they'll
never get to know!

16:58.430 --> 17:01.610
It's horrible. You're right.

17:01.690 --> 17:03.400
But when I'm done,
we'll finally be able to

17:03.480 --> 17:05.190
break free of the cycle
we've been trapped in

17:05.280 --> 17:06.980
for two thousand years.

17:07.070 --> 17:09.110
Our long history of hate

17:09.200 --> 17:12.990
will be buried in the
ruins of civilization.

17:13.080 --> 17:15.490
The MPs. They plan to
make you bear children

17:15.580 --> 17:18.410
to be sacrificed for the island.

17:18.500 --> 17:21.120
They'll keep forcing children
to eat their parents.

17:21.210 --> 17:23.170
I won't let them.

17:29.090 --> 17:31.390
Eren, please. Don't do it.

17:31.470 --> 17:34.430
I'll have no choice
but to try and stop you.

17:34.510 --> 17:36.720
'Cause if I don't,
I'll have to live with

17:36.810 --> 17:38.640
the world's blood on my hands.

17:38.720 --> 17:39.890
And I can't.

17:39.980 --> 17:42.190
I know it's a burden,
but if you can bear it

17:42.270 --> 17:44.110
till I've got
the Founder's power,

17:44.190 --> 17:46.150
I'll make you forget
you ever knew it was coming.

17:46.230 --> 17:47.280
How could I, though?

17:47.360 --> 17:49.190
I know you can,
'cause you're the person

17:49.280 --> 17:51.860
who saved my life
back in that cavern.

17:51.950 --> 17:54.830
The worst girl who ever lived.

17:58.240 --> 17:59.830
Headaches, huh?

17:59.910 --> 18:02.040
Well. I doubt
there's a connection.

18:02.120 --> 18:04.130
It would have to be
some genetic illness,

18:04.210 --> 18:05.960
but Mister Ksaver and
Marley's researchers

18:06.040 --> 18:07.710
would have made note of that.

18:07.800 --> 18:09.960
Our studies do indicate
the Ackermann bloodline

18:10.050 --> 18:11.920
carries some odd quirks.

18:12.010 --> 18:13.260
Powers that activate when their

18:13.340 --> 18:15.930
survival instincts
are triggered.

18:16.010 --> 18:20.100
But this theory that she's
reflexively guarding her "host"?

18:21.270 --> 18:24.980
To be honest, it seems
a little far-fetched to me.

18:25.060 --> 18:28.320
I think it's far simpler
than you're making it, Eren.

18:28.400 --> 18:29.980
There are straightforward
explanations

18:30.070 --> 18:32.070
for all the behaviors
you're describing

18:32.150 --> 18:34.950
that have nothing to do with
genetics or conditioning.

18:35.030 --> 18:36.490
She doesn't slaughter
Titans out of some

18:36.580 --> 18:39.870
inborn compulsion
to keep you alive.

18:39.950 --> 18:42.620
She does it because
she adores you.

18:44.540 --> 18:46.290
Hey, Eren, listen.

18:46.380 --> 18:50.210
[ZEKE] Well? What do you think
you're going to say to her?

18:50.300 --> 18:52.340
That's not a serious
question, is it?

18:52.420 --> 18:53.840
Even if everything goes right,

18:53.920 --> 18:56.470
I've only got four
more years to live.

18:56.550 --> 18:59.470
What would you think
about me having a child?

19:01.060 --> 19:07.610
[EREN groaning]

19:11.780 --> 19:14.320
[EREN groaning]

19:15.450 --> 19:17.160
My life's end date is set,

19:17.240 --> 19:19.870
but my friends will keep living
long after I'm gone.

19:19.950 --> 19:24.000
[EREN groaning]

19:25.080 --> 19:27.290
[EREN]
And that's what I want.

19:27.380 --> 19:29.710
[EREN groaning]

19:30.630 --> 19:32.340
[EREN]
What I need.

19:40.810 --> 19:45.560
[EREN] For them to live
long, happy lives.

19:54.740 --> 19:57.240
[ADMIRAL 87A]
An allied global fleet.

19:57.320 --> 20:00.120
Nearly all of the largest
guns ever manufactured

20:00.200 --> 20:02.540
have been gathered
from across the globe,

20:02.620 --> 20:06.960
here, today,
off the coast of Marley.

20:07.040 --> 20:09.540
The combined brainpower
of the world's nations

20:09.630 --> 20:13.170
is focused entirely on
resolving this shared crisis.

20:13.250 --> 20:15.300
It took nothing short
of a miracle to even

20:15.380 --> 20:17.970
assemble a fleet
of this magnitude.

20:18.050 --> 20:23.680
And by that miracle alone,
humanity still clings to hope.

20:27.480 --> 20:31.860
[ADMIRAL 87A] For salvation
from this rumbling.

21:18.610 --> 21:19.860
[Gasps]

21:41.720 --> 21:43.100
[ADMIRAL 87A gasps]

22:34.310 --> 22:39.070
[MARLEYAN SOLDIERS gasping]

22:49.120 --> 22:50.580
[Gasps]

22:57.590 --> 22:59.960
[MARLEYAN SOLDIER 87B]
Is that...? Yeah.

23:00.050 --> 23:04.130
It could only be...
the Attack Titan!

23:05.220 --> 23:07.800
[MARLEYAN SOLDIERS gasp]

23:16.100 --> 23:18.360
[EREN]
I'll kill them all.

23:30.700 --> 23:33.160
[EREN]
Every last one.

23:34.620 --> 23:37.040
[EREN]
The world over.
